    {
      "i": 7,
      "title": "Budget and alerts",
      "detail": "A Cloud Billing budget of $11 a month on this project (the Cloud Run estimate rounded up, at least $5), with email alerts to the billing admins at 50%, 90% and 100% of actual spend and at 100% of the forecast: `gcloud billing budgets create --billing-account=BILLING_ACCOUNT_ID --display-name=\"rails-heroku on Cloud Run\" --budget-amount=11USD --calendar-period=month --filter-projects=projects/PROJECT_ID --threshold-rule=percent=0.5 --threshold-rule=percent=0.9 --threshold-rule=percent=1.0 --threshold-rule=percent=1.0,basis=forecasted-spend` (the currency is the billing account's own; `--notifications-rule-pubsub-topic` adds a Pub/Sub topic for automated reactions). It needs Billing Account Administrator or Billing Account Costs Manager, or the project's owner for a budget on this project only. It changes billing settings: the agent shows the command, the person approves, and it runs with the person's own gcloud. How budgets work: https://exodus.elim.io/blog/budget-alerts-and-the-billing-export. Then a spend cap of $22 a month, a second budget that stops Cloud Run instead of only warning: in the console, Billing, Budgets & alerts, Create new budget, Spend cap enforcement, this project, the service Cloud Run, the amount $22 (or the Cloud Billing Budget API with `spendCap.inputState` CONFIGURED, the service `services/152E-C115-5142` and `creditTypesTreatment` EXCLUDE_ALL_CREDITS). Past the cap, Cloud Run in this project pauses until the 1st of the next month or until the person lifts the cap: services answer 5xx, jobs and worker pools stop, nothing is deleted. It counts gross list-price costs before savings and credits and fires before the bill shows them, so it sits at twice the budget, at least $10, not at the estimate. Spend caps are monthly, for one project and one service; alerts go to the billing admins and project owners at 50%, 80% and 100%. It needs `billing.budgets.configureSpendCap` on the billing account, or `billing.resourcebudgets.configureSpendCap` on the project. Turning the app off at a ceiling is the person's call: the agent explains it, shows the steps and waits for a yes or no.",
      "effort": "S",
      "phase": 3,
      "status": "todo"
    },
